{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Vectors, Matrices & Operations Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Vector class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Vector:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, data):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.data = list(data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.size = len(self.data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __repr__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return f\"Vector({self.data})\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __add__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return Vector([a + b for a, b in zip(self.data, other.data)])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __sub__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return Vector([a - b for a, b in zip(self.data, other.data)])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __mul__(self, scalar):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return Vector([x * scalar for x in self.data])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def dot(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return sum(a * b for a, b in zip(self.data, other.data))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def magnitude(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return sum(x ** 2 for x in self.data) ** 0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Matrix class with core operations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Matrix:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, data):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.data = [list(row) for row in data]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.rows = len(self.data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.cols = len(self.data[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.shape = (self.rows, self.cols)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __repr__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rows_str = \"\\n  \".join(str(row) for row in self.data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return f\"Matrix({self.shape}):\\n  {rows_str}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __add__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return Matrix(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            [self.data[i][j] + other.data[i][j] for j in range(self.cols)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for i in range(self.rows)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __sub__(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return Matrix(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            [self.data[i][j] - other.data[i][j] for j in range(self.cols)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for i in range(self.rows)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def scalar_multiply(self, scalar):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return Matrix(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            [self.data[i][j] * scalar for j in range(self.cols)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for i in range(self.rows)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def element_wise_multiply(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return Matrix(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            [self.data[i][j] * other.data[i][j] for j in range(self.cols)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for i in range(self.rows)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def matmul(self, other):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return Matrix(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                sum(self.data[i][k] * other.data[k][j] for k in range(self.cols))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for j in range(other.cols)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for i in range(self.rows)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def transpose(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return Matrix(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            [self.data[j][i] for j in range(self.rows)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for i in range(self.cols)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def determinant(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if self.shape == (1, 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return self.data[0][0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if self.shape == (2, 2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return self.data[0][0] * self.data[1][1] - self.data[0][1] * self.data[1][0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        det = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j in range(self.cols):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            minor = Matrix(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                [self.data[i][k] for k in range(self.cols) if k != j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for i in range(1, self.rows)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            det += ((-1) ** j) * self.data[0][j] * minor.determinant()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return det"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def inverse_2x2(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        det = self.determinant()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if det == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            raise ValueError(\"Matrix is singular, no inverse exists\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return Matrix(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            [self.data[1][1] / det, -self.data[0][1] / det],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            [-self.data[1][0] / det, self.data[0][0] / det]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    @staticmethod"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def identity(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return Matrix(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            [1 if i == j else 0 for j in range(n)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for i in range(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: See it work"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A = Matrix([[1, 2], [3, 4]])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "B = Matrix([[5, 6], [7, 8]])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"A + B =\", (A + B).data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"A @ B =\", A.matmul(B).data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"A^T =\", A.transpose().data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"det(A) =\", A.determinant())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"A^-1 =\", A.inverse_2x2().data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "I = Matrix.identity(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"A @ A^-1 =\", A.matmul(A.inverse_2x2()).data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Connect to neural networks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "inputs = Matrix([[0.5], [0.8], [0.2]])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "weights = Matrix(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    [random.uniform(-1, 1) for _ in range(3)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "bias = Matrix([[0.1], [0.1]])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def relu_matrix(m):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return Matrix([[max(0, val) for val in row] for row in m.data])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pre_activation = weights.matmul(inputs) + bias"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "output = relu_matrix(pre_activation)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Input shape: {inputs.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Weight shape: {weights.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Output shape: {output.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Output: {output.data}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This is a single dense layer: `output = relu(W @ x + b)`. Every dense layer in every neural network does exactly this."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Verify the inverse.** Multiply `A @ A.inverse_2x2()` and confirm you get the identity matrix. Try it with three different 2x2 matrices. What happens when the determinant is zero?\n\n2. **Implement 3x3 inverse.** Extend the Matrix class to compute inverses for 3x3 matrices using the adjugate method. Test it against NumPy's `np.linalg.inv`.\n\n3. **Build a two-layer network.** Using only your Matrix class (no NumPy), create a two-layer neural network: input (3) -> hidden (4) -> output (2). Initialize random weights, run a forward pass, and verify all shapes are correct."
      ]
    }
